From db216d30059d988c5ae2ba45c11393986749347e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:34:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: identify Tor control authentication and lifecycle
 events

Convert13 static Tor control Info diagnostics to stable events. Preserve exact
human text, Info severity (including existing Error wording), ALL category and
all authentication/disconnect/thread branches. No password, nonce, key, hostname
or address values added. Dynamic/continuation consumers remain separately
reviewed/deferred; this does not claim the whole Tor subsystem is converted.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py0.51.0; reviewed catalog committed here):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/tor-control-static-lifecycle.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/tor-control-applied.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/torcontrol.cpp

Validation:15 converter fixtures including all13 mappings/exact text/severity,
idempotence after formatting, event lint13 and diff check PASS. Native compile
and runtime are pending the normal isolated build; no new fields or APIs.
Tier:shared eCash, V2 inherits.

